            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Right, this was on purpose.  We shouldn't be publishing registries we don't implement."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Hmm.  What's the best way for us to figure this out?  I can make another config-file of sorts that we can specify which ones we actually need.  Or, I can go back to this file being static for the Redfish standard ones and then only the dbus ones we generate.  I was trying to make the paths as least different as possible, so that's why I put this in place.\n\nIs it a big concern if we do expose registries even if we don't use them?  Are you concerned about the resulting image size or is there a Redfish-reason for not exposing registries you don't emit?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> if we do expose registries even if we don't use them? \n\nYes, because this is how systems \"advertise\" to clients what they support so they can filter/set profiles accordingly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Exposing registries openbmc doesn't support is still a breaking change with this patch and needs fixed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Any reason this output is random?  Could we make it alphabetical?  Generally we enforce that for collections."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I will fix this in the preceding commit.  We need to use an `map` rather than an `unordered_map` so that iteration is ordered."
                }
            ],
